<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for omnidb-server specifically — NOT the same file as
  entitlements.plist (used for the main OmniDB executable and the outer
  .app bundle). Learned the hard way: signing omnidb-server with its own
  full app-sandbox entitlement (like entitlements.plist declares) crashes
  it instantly with SIGTRAP ("Trace/BPT trap: 5"), inside
  libsecinit_appsandbox, before main() ever runs — confirmed via
  ~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/omnidb-server-*.ips. Root cause: App
  Sandbox's own initialization expects the sandboxing process to BE the
  bundle's declared CFBundleExecutable (Info.plist says "OmniDB", not
  "omnidb-server") — a second executable living in the same Contents/MacOS/
  cannot independently establish its own sandbox that way, even though nothing
  stops it from being codesigned with that entitlement in the first place.

  com.apple.security.inherit is the correct entitlement for exactly this
  shape of helper binary: a child process (see wails-app/backend.go's
  startBackend, which os/exec.Command()s this binary) that should run
  within whatever sandbox its parent (the main, properly-bundled OmniDB
  executable) already has, rather than trying to establish an independent
  one of its own. It needs no explicit network.client/network.server/etc of
  its own — those are already granted to the sandbox it inherits.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.inherit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
